{#
   One token of a target list — a transition's `target`, a state's initial
   transition, a `<history>`'s default — as the C++ policy spells it.

   A `<history>` is not a state and has no State enumerator: it is named in
   the policy's History enum, and the engine's entry procedures dereference it
   to what it recorded or to its default. Every other token is a State.

   `history_states` is the model's map of history ids, passed in rather than
   read from the caller's context because an imported macro does not see it.
#}
{% macro entry_target(token, history_states) -%}
{%- if token in history_states -%}EntryTargetT::onHistory(History::{{ token | capitalize }})
{%- else -%}EntryTargetT::onState(State::{{ token | capitalize }})
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}
